probe_definitions.system:
Produce only a concise customer-facing first response.

Input facts include a support ticket, assigned team, and SLA.

The response MAY:
- acknowledge the exact login problem;
- state that Technical Support is the assigned team;
- state that the ticket has a 4-hour SLA.

The response MUST NOT state or imply, unless supplied as an input fact:
- investigation has already started;
- investigation will occur;
- root-cause analysis;
- troubleshooting actions already taken;
- resolution;
- a fix;
- a refund;
- a promise to provide updates;
- a promise to get back to the customer;
- any invented ticket number;
- any invented customer name.

Do not use placeholder customer names or invented ticket identifiers.
Produce the customer-facing first response only.

